    "Compliments": [
      ["Todo estuvo delicioso.","TOH-doh ehs-TOO-boh deh-lee-SYOH-soh","Everything was delicious.","Say it to the host or cook after a meal; fine with tú or usted."],
      ["Cocinas muy bien.","koh-SEE-nahs mwee byehn","You're a really good cook.","tú form. To someone you call usted: Usted cocina muy bien."],
      ["¡Bien hecho!","byehn EH-choh","Well done!","For anyone, any age; hecho never changes."],
      ["¡Qué bien lo haces!","keh byehn loh AH-sehs","You're really good at this!","Literally: how well you do it. To someone you call usted: ¡Qué bien lo hace!"],
      ["¡Qué buena idea!","keh BWEH-nah ee-DEH-ah","What a great idea!","buena agrees with idea (feminine). Fine with anyone."],
      ["Eres muy amable.","EH-rehs mwee ah-MAH-bleh","You're very kind.","amable is the same for men and women. To someone you call usted: Usted es muy amable."],
      ["Eres muy chistoso.","EH-rehs mwee chees-TOH-soh","You're really funny.","To a woman: Eres muy chistosa. gracioso is understood everywhere too."],
      ["Eres muy trabajador.","EH-rehs mwee trah-bah-hah-DOHR","You're very hard-working.","To a woman: Eres muy trabajadora. A warm compliment, at work or at home."],
      ["¡Qué bonita casa tienes!","keh boh-NEE-tah KAH-sah TYEH-nehs","What a lovely home you have!","bonita agrees with casa. To someone you call usted: ¡Qué bonita casa tiene!"],
      ["Te queda muy bien.","teh KEH-dah mwee byehn","That looks great on you.","About clothes. For a plural item: Te quedan muy bien. To someone you call usted: Le queda muy bien."],
      ["¡Qué bonita foto!","keh boh-NEE-tah FOH-toh","What a nice photo!","foto is feminine (short for fotografía), so bonita, not bonito."],
      ["Hablas muy bien español.","AH-blahs mwee byehn ehs-pah-NYOHL","You speak Spanish really well.","What people will say to you. To someone you call usted: Habla muy bien español."],
      ["Gracias, qué amable.","GRAH-syahs keh ah-MAH-bleh","Thanks, that's kind of you.","The normal reply to a compliment in Latin America: accept it and thank the person."],
      ["Gracias, pero todavía me falta mucho.","GRAH-syahs PEH-roh toh-dah-BEE-ah meh FAHL-tah MOO-choh","Thanks, but I still have a lot to learn.","The usual modest reply when someone praises your Spanish; a plain gracias is fine too."]
    ],
