      ["Why is it buenos días but buenas noches?",["Morning greetings are always masculine","días is masculine and noches is feminine, and the word for good matches each","buenas is the polite form","No reason: either form works with either word"],1,"bueno agrees with the noun: días is masculine, noches is feminine."],
      ["How do you say My name is Carlos?",["Me llamo es Carlos.","Mi llamo Carlos.","Me llamo Carlos.","Yo llamo Carlos."],2,"me llamo already means my name is; it needs no es, and the small word is me, not mi."]
